    "title": "A Beloved Saga's Perfect Ending",
    "text": "Here’s a breakdown of the information provided in the text, organized for clarity:\nAbout the Film:\nTitle: Downton Abbey: The Grand Finale\nSetting: 1930\nPurpose: To provide a concluding chapter to the Downton Abbey story (spanning 14 years of TV and film).\nThemes: Societal change, subtle humor, dramatic flair.\nReview Summary:\nThe Bottom line: “An elegant farewell.”\nRelease Date: Friday, Sept. 12\nDirector: Simon Curtis\nScreenwriter: Julian Fellowes\nRating: PG\nRuntime: 2 hours 23 minutes\nCast (a very extensive list!):\nSimon Russell Beale\nHugh Bonneville\nLaura Carmichael\nJim carter\nRaquel Cassidy\nBrendan Coyle\nMichelle Dockery\nKevin Doyle\nMichael Fox\nJoanne Froggatt\nPaul Giamatti\nHarry Hadden-Paton\nRobert james-Collier\nAllen Leech\nPhyllis Logan\nElizabeth McGovern\nSophie McShera\nLesley Nicol\nAlessandro Nivola\nDominic West\nPenelope Wilton\nArty Froushan\nJoely Richardson\nPaul Copley\nDouglas Reith\nPlot Points (Early Narrative):\nthe film opens with characters attending Noel Coward’s operetta Bitter Sweet in London.\nA high-society ball is attended by Robert, Cora, and Mary.\nNews of Mary’s divorce becomes public, leading to her being ostracized from the ball by the hostess (Joely Richardson).",
